        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "18e56191-b389-5332-b06a-e84c9d5e0189",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Elton, Andrew Lloyd Webber, Glenn Slater, Frederick Forsyth, Summer Strallen, Don Black, Christopher Hampton, Amy Powers\n- Works: The Young Ones, Blackadder, We Will Rock You, Love Never Dies, The Phantom of the Opera, The Sound of Music, As If We Never Said Goodbye\n- Topics: alternative comedy, musicals, West End, London Palladium\n\nFacts:\n- Ben Elton was born on 3 May 1959 and is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor, and director.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton was part of London's alternative comedy movement.\n- In the 1980s, Ben Elton became a writer on The Young Ones and Blackadder while continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\n- Ben Elton wrote the musical We Will Rock You, which premiered in 2002.\n- Love Never Dies is a romantic musical with music by Andrew Lloyd Webber and a book by Andrew Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth, and Glenn Slater, with lyrics by Glenn Slater.\n- Summer Strallen played Meg Giry in the West End production of Love Never Dies.\n- Ben Elton wrote the musical Love Never Dies, which premiered in 2010 as the sequel to The Phantom of the Opera.\n- Summer Strallen also played Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of The Sound of Music at the London Palladium.\n- As If We Never Said Goodbye was written by Don Black, Christopher Hampton, and Andrew Lloyd Webber, with additional lyrics by Amy Powers.\n- Ben Elton has published 15 novels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4cad8a9f-e7b0-535f-af4d-b72aef19e6ce",
        "text": "Page: Ben Elton. Sentence: Benjamin Charles Elton (born 3 May 1959) is an English comedian, author, playwright, actor and director.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: He was a part of London's alternative comedy movement of the 1980s and became a writer on series such as \"The Young Ones\" and \"Blackadder\", as well as continuing as a stand-up comedian on stage and television.\nPage: Ben Elton. Sentence: Since then he has published 15 novels and written the musicals \"We Will Rock You\" (2002) and \"Love Never Dies\" (2010), the sequel to \"The Phantom of the Opera\".\nPage: Love Never Dies (musical). Sentence: Love Never Dies is a romantic musical composed by Andrew Lloyd Webber with lyrics by Glenn Slater and a book by Lloyd Webber, Ben Elton, Frederick Forsyth and Slater.\nPage: Summer Strallen. Sentence: Her most notable theatre credits include Meg Giry in the West End production of \"Love Never Dies\" and Maria von Trapp in Andrew Lloyd Webber's revival of \"The Sound of Music\" at the London Palladium.\nPage: As If We Never Said Goodbye. Sentence: It is written by Don Black, Christopher Hampton (with additional lyrics by Amy Powers), and Andrew Lloyd Webber.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
